    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0342" n="330" xml:id="pg330"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/1986: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-02-11T22:00:00-04:00">February 11,
                            1943—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>76. Your 134, February 5. If occasion arises, you may advise your British and
                    Russian colleagues that Department, on basis of its present information, does
                    not regard Seyid Zia-ed-Din Tabatabai as a suitable person to head Iranian
                    Government. Our opinion is based upon both his record and the fact that he has
                    been away from Iran for past 20 years. Accordingly, we would not be disposed to
                    encourage any movement for his return to power.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
